WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.439
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.
Today’s video is like the human heart

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:07.200
and barbershop quartet harmonies: it comes
to you in four parts. Part 1: The Holidays.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.740
Hank, here in the United States
there are several holidays coming up.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.460
And this year both Christmas Eve and New Year’s Eve
fall on Tuesdays, and I will be taking

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.960
both those days off.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.420
Part 2: related. I've been thinking
about burnout a lot lately.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.610
I’m not really burnt out at the moment,
but I am starting to think differently about

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.699
the role work plays in my life.

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.859
Ever since I was about 22, I've worked
many nights and most weekends.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.540
I don’t recommend working that way and I
don’t need to, but I've continued to do it anyway.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.600
My central goal for the next decade is to do
fewer things that the world constructs as “work”

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.830
and more things that are valuable but not usually
imagined as “work,” like spending time with family

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:47.140
and doing the dishes and sleeping and reading and
volunteering my time and talents to causes I care about.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.880
I’m just saying that out loud in the hopes
that it will make me accountable.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.680
Part 3: The Project for Awesome.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.060
So Hank, back in 2007 when we first came up with
the idea for the Foundation to Decrease Worldsuck,

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.280
it was mostly a joke, like we "decreased worldsuck"
by paying for people to go to their first concerts.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.800
Which is a value added to the universe, I
think, but maybe not the most efficient one.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.860
But then the Project for Awesome started to
grow, and the Foundation to Decrease Worldsuck

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.620
became a real charity that can accept tax
deductible donations despite its very silly name.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.460
And last year, the Project for Awesome raised
its ten millionth dollar for charity.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.580
The P4A is my favorite time of the year, and
I can't wait for the strange mix of exhaustion

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.120
and exhilaration it brings.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:29.160
The 13th annual—how is that possible—
Project for Awesome will happen this year

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.400
between noon Eastern Time on Friday December 6th
and noon Eastern on Sunday December 8th,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.970
but the Indiegogo will launch this year
on December 3rd.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:41.740
There will be many amazing perks available—more on
those next week—and because the Project for Awesome

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.580
is a volunteer-run organization, except for
credit card fees and the cost of making

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.520
and shipping physical perks,
all donations go to charity.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.580
As in past years, during the first half
of the Project for Awesome,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.160
we’ll be raising money for pre-selected charities,
Save the Children and Partners in Health,

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.380
both of which our community has worked with for over
a decade, and both of which have excellent reputations

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.500
for reaching and assisting the most
vulnerable people in the world.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.700
I should mention that this year’s P4A fundraising
will be entirely separate from the project

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.860
we announced a couple of months ago
with Partners in Health Sierra Leone.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.620
Over 3,000 of you have joined us in donating to support
the strengthening of Sierra Leone’s healthcare system,

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.100
and we are so grateful and excited to watch
that progress over the next several years.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.540
But during this year’s P4A, as in past years,
we’re raising so-called “unrestricted funds,”

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.620
which allows PIH and Save the Children to
spend the money wherever it’s most needed.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.100
Partners in Health, for instance, might need
money to support a clinic in the Navajo nation

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.920
or to buy medical supplies in Haiti. They know better
than we do where the funding gaps are,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:41.230
and unrestricted funds are really important to charities,
so we’re keeping the Sierra Leone project separate.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.470
If you have any questions about this or about
anything, please leave them in the comments!

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.220
It occurs to me that someday YouTube will probably
move the comments section to like a sidebar,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.300
and then it will look to people like
I’m just pointing at my pants.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.860
And then it occurs to me that someday, YouTube will
not exist at all. But back to the Project for Awesome!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.200
Right, okay, so during the second half of
the Project for Awesome, as in past years

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.400
we will be raising money for charities
chosen by you.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.540
YOU make a great video in support of a charity
you think deserves a grant

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.620
and then upload it on Friday December 6th,

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:12.240
and if people vote for it at projectforawesome.com,
that charity might receive part of the funds

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.760
raised during the second half
of the Project for Awesome.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.910
So we’re counting on you to make great videos and pick
worthy charities. Alright, let’s talk about money!

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.320
Hank and I will be matching the first $150,000
raised in this year’s Project for Awesome.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.560
And I know lots of you have donated to lots
of causes, so really no pressure,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:36.280
but if you would like to join that matching fund,
you can email us at ftdws@complexly.com.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.040
That email address is also in the dooblydoo
and in the comments below.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.680
If you are able to join the matching fund,
you will be thanked profusely

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.500
and it really does help drive donations.
Okay, Part 4!

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.880
For making it to the end of an update video,
you win a picture of my brother and me as reindeer—

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:54.460
one of the amazing months of
the 2020 Project for Awesome calendar.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.300
Rudolph, I’ll see you on Friday.

